# Repo-root attributes.
#
# Plugin/ and UnityProject/ each already declare `* text=auto`; this extends the same
# normalisation to the root and to AssetSources/, which had no coverage at all.
#
# WHY THE EXPLICIT BINARY LIST BELOW: core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so with
# `text=auto` git decides text-vs-binary by sniffing content. Anything it guesses wrong
# gets CRLF injected on checkout, which silently corrupts an audio file, a Blender scene,
# or the asset bundle. The files listed here are declared binary so no guess is involved.

* text=auto

# The asset bundle has NO extension, so it is the one most exposed to a bad guess.
gargoyleassets binary
*.bundle binary

# Audio (shipped OGG + Audacity project sources, which are SQLite databases)
*.ogg binary
*.aup3 binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary

# Art sources and images
*.blend binary
*.blend1 binary
*.xcf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.tga binary
*.psd binary

# Documents and archives
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.zip binary

# Assemblies and debug symbols
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.exe binary

# Text formats that must keep LF regardless of platform
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
